## One thing worth flagging

Step 7's subagent legitimately reached 72/72. My orchestrator-side re-verification initially produced a **false total-failure** because I simplified the sweep command to `bash start.sh` (relying on an outer `cd`). The runner's per-test restart hook (`pytest_plugin._parse_command`) re-runs the start command from pytest's own cwd — the project root, where `start.sh` doesn't exist — so every per-test restart failed and every test ERROR'd at setup. A `--skip-lifecycle` control run against one persistent server passed 72/72, isolating the fault to the restart command; re-running with the `cd <impl> &&`-embedded form (the form the skill specifies) gave a clean 8×72/72.

This is exactly the "sweep start-command cwd gotcha" already in memory — the note held up. I left a record of the diagnosis in `worklog.md` so the trail is durable.

The implementation, tests, and all three PRD variants are in place and the suite is green and flake-free.
